exit 0
--- stdout
Docs · 177 asks                                                        49 topics

agents  add a sub-agent for every project or for one, choose the model it
  runs, and remove it
  see which sub-agents exist and their models
    → tofu agents
  add a sub-agent to this project
    → tofu agents add <name> --description "<what it does>" --model <source/model>
  add a sub-agent to every project
    → tofu agents add --global <name> --description "<what it does>" --model <source/model>
  run a sub-agent on another model
    → tofu agents set <name> <source/model>
  remove a sub-agent I added
    → tofu agents remove <name>
  set up three sub-agents at once, each on its own model
    → tofu agents add <name> --description "<what it does>" --model <source/model>, once per sub-agent
  check each plan the lead sets against what I asked
    → tofu settings set planAdvisor shadow
  stop the plan advisor
    → tofu settings set planAdvisor off
  which tools a sub-agent with no agent named gets
    → tofu tool list --agent unnamed
  change the tool list of a sub-agent with no agent named
    → write .tofu/agents/unnamed.md with a tools line

api-keys  tofu login --status shows each API key's calls, tokens and cost with
  where the cost came from, the limits and balance the provider reports, and
  what that provider does not report
  how much has my API key spent, and what limit is left
    → tofu login --status

asking  how the lead puts a decision to you with options and a recommended
  one, what auto and ask do with it, and when it cannot ask
  let a question wait longer for my answer
    → tofu settings set askPersonWaitSeconds 600
  close a question without choosing and answer it later
    → pick return, the last row of the form

boardy-rules  who may change a ticket on a boardy board, how other sessions
  ask through triage, how a ticket moves boards, and hooks that check, nudge or
  act before and after any board event
  let a session change tickets on the board
    → tofu boardy manager add <session>
  see what other sessions asked the board for
    → tofu boardy triage list
  answer a held bypass of a board rule
    → tofu boardy bypass answer <B> yes --why "<reason>"

boardy-views  saved views over a board's ticket files, a report built from
  tickets and events, epics, milestones and sprints as files, and the boardy
  methods on tofu serve
  show only this sprint's tickets
    → tofu boardy view
  sum up the board
    → tofu boardy report --since 7d

boardy  boards of tickets kept as markdown files under the tofu home, numbered
  under a lock, moved through statuses and checked by lint
  keep a ticket board for this project
    → tofu boardy init --key DEMO
  run my agents from board tickets
    → tofu settings set projectManagement boardy
  keep what I asked word for word, with the tickets cut from it
    → tofu boardy request new "<your words>" --tickets <A,B>
  review a board request against my own words
    → tofu boardy request review <R> pass --note "<what you checked>"
  record a before capture of how things work before a change
    → tofu boardy log <id> --before "<what you ran and what it printed>"
  research an epic before it takes tickets
    → tofu boardy epic research <ID> "<note>", then tofu boardy epic design <ID> "<design>" --first "<smallest first version>"
  name the skills a ticket's sub-agent loads
    → tofu boardy set <id> --skills <a,b>

browser  how tofu reads and drives your Chrome tabs, the tofu tab group, the
  badge, and what tofu never does there
  connect tofu to Chrome
    → tofu browser install
  let the model read the Chrome tabs tofu can reach
    → tofu settings set browser read
  let the model click and type in the tabs tofu can reach
    → tofu settings set browser drive
  take the browser tools away from the model
    → tofu settings set browser off
  let jev pick each browser step toward a whole goal instead of the model
    → tofu settings set browserDriver goal
  allow fewer actions in one browser task
    → tofu settings set browserSteps 10

calibration  how tofu calibrate fits a decision point's cut on labelled cases,
  checks it on a held-out half and a rerun, and writes the lock that lets the
  point leave shadow
  calibrate a decision point on labelled cases
    → tofu calibrate <rule@version> --cases <cases.jsonl> --split <split.json> --dry-run

code-review  how /code-review asks the lead to review one change for what it
  breaks now and later, inside and outside the diff, and report each finding
  with path:line, severity and the mechanism
  review my change for what it breaks
    → /code-review in the app, or /code-review HEAD~1..HEAD for one range

commands  every slash command the app's composer takes, how /skill off drops a
  skill your words loaded, how /compact shrinks the history the next turn
  carries, how /fork and /branch start a new line by hand, how /undo puts files
  back, and how /permissions lists and revokes a standing answer
  free room in the context before the next turn
    → /compact in the app, between turns
  undo what the last turn changed
    → tofu undo, or /undo in the app
  fork the conversation now and start a fresh line
    → /fork in the app
  branch from one of my earlier messages and keep the old line
    → /branch in the app to list your messages, then /branch N
  open a side chat beside the session
    → /side in the app
  take back an always or never answer I gave
    → /permissions in the app, then /permissions revoke <n>

context  how a long conversation stays under its target, when old results are
  trimmed, when a session forks, and why neither breaks the prompt cache
  why did my session fork, and how full is the context
    → tofu context

cron  jobs that post a prompt into the session on a timer or after each turn,
  how to change one, and the history of every change
  repeat a prompt every few minutes
    → /loop 10m check the build
  keep working until a test passes
    → /goal make the test pass --until "go test ./..."
  change when a scheduled job fires
    → /cron edit c1 --schedule "every 30m" --reason "the build is stable"
  stop a scheduled job
    → /cron delete c1
  I am away, keep working without asking me
    → tell the lead you are leaving; it calls cron with action away
  I am back, ask me again
    → tell the lead you are back; it calls cron with action back

doctor  what tofu doctor checks, what each line it prints means, and what to
