tool  list the tools a run offers and run one call the way the loop runs it,
  printing the exact text the model would receive
  run one tool call by hand and see what the model would read
    → tofu tool read '{"path":"README.md"}' --dir .

tools-change  what codemod, scaffold, format and deps give the model: one code
  shape rewritten everywhere on the syntax tree, a new file shaped like a
  sibling, the project's formatter on the files named, and a dependency added
  after its license, size and advisories are read
  rewrite one code shape everywhere without touching strings
    → tofu tool codemod '{"lang":"go","pattern":"t.Fatalf($$$ARGS)","rewrite":"t.Errorf($$$ARGS)"}' --dir .
  make a new file shaped like an existing one
    → tofu tool scaffold '{"kind":"type","name":"Invoice","like":"order.go"}' --dir .
  format only the files i changed
    → tofu tool format '{"paths":["label.go"]}' --dir .
  add a dependency after checking its license and advisories
    → tofu tool deps '{"mode":"add","package":"github.com/google/uuid"}' --dir .
  which dependencies have a newer release
    → tofu tool deps '{"mode":"outdated"}' --dir .

tools-checks  what test, typecheck, mutate, read, write, edit, bash and shell
  give the model, and how to see it for yourself

tools-code  what symbols, map, api and eval give the model: where a name is
  declared and who calls it, what a change reaches, what matters for a task, a
  dependency at its pinned version, and what an expression returns

tools-context  what context, budget, forget, note, digest, done, claims and
  the review agent give the model
  how long will this work take
    → ask the lead; it answers with estimate_time
  how long until a running sub-agent finishes
    → ask the lead; it calls estimate_time with the sub-agent's id

tools-debug  what debug gives the model: a Go or Python program or test run
  under dlv or debugpy, stopped at a line, with the values there, and every call
  of one Go function
  see the values on one call of a function without print lines
    → tofu tool debug '{"steps":["start test TestTill","break till.go:14 --if t.rung == 3","run","eval cents","stop"]}' --dir .
  list every call of a go function with its arguments and result
    → tofu tool debug '{"steps":["start test TestTill","trace orders.(*Till).Ring","stop"]}' --dir .

tools-work  what plan, history, fetch, web_search, env, http, record, profile,
  shape, db, spawn, race, ask_person and heads_up give the model

tools  what each tool gives the model, grouped by job, which page says more
  about each group, and how to see a result for yourself
  run the tests of one package and see only what failed
    → tofu tool test '{"path":"."}' --dir .
  check a report against the calls the session made
    → tofu tool claims '{"report":"All tests pass."}' --dir . --session head
  which tools does the review agent get
    → tofu tool list --agent review
  typecheck go, rust or python code
    → tofu tool typecheck '{"path":"."}' --dir .
  read the lines around one function
    → tofu tool read '{"path":"order.go","at":"Total"}' --dir .
  who calls this function, through every import alias
    → tofu tool symbols '{"name":"total"}' --dir .
  what else must change if I change this type
    → tofu tool symbols '{"name":"Order","mode":"impact"}' --dir .
  rename a function everywhere it is used
    → tofu tool symbols '{"name":"total","path":"src/pricing.rs","mode":"rename","to":"amount"}' --dir .
  which files matter for this task
    → tofu tool map '{"task":"Discounted returns 650, want 675"}' --dir .
  what does this dependency look like at the version we pinned
    → tofu tool api '{"package":"github.com/pelletier/go-toml/v2","name":"NewDecoder"}' --dir .
  can this project build here, and which env keys are missing
    → tofu tool env '{}' --dir .
  see what is in the project database without writing to it
    → tofu tool db '{"env":"DATABASE_URL"}' --dir .
  get a type for a json sample
    → tofu tool shape '{"path":"orders.json"}' --dir .
  what does a sub-agent usually cost before I start one
    → tofu tool spawn '{"estimate":true,"agent":"go-dev"}' --dir .
  try two approaches at once and keep the one that passes
    → tofu docs tools
  tell me something during a turn without stopping it
    → tofu tool heads_up '{"level":"info","line":"the full test run takes about two minutes"}' --dir .
  what does the model see filling its own window
    → tofu tool context '{}' --dir . --session head
  what has this session cost, by turn and by agent
    → tofu tool budget '{}' --dir . --session head
  let the model ask a cheap model about one long result
    → tofu settings set modelTier.dumb <source/model>

